WEBVTT

00:02.310 --> 00:04.780
Eastern Japan General Hospital

00:02.310 --> 00:04.780
Eastern Japan General Hospital

00:06.990 --> 00:08.950
<b>Exam Room 3</b>

00:06.990 --> 00:08.950
<b>Neurosurgery Dept.</b>

00:06.990 --> 00:08.950
<b>Attending Physician Usaki Mofu</b>

00:08.950 --> 00:11.160
Your test results are in.

00:11.600 --> 00:13.300
Kamonohashi Ron-san,

00:13.300 --> 00:18.870
your involuntary pressuring of perpetrators 
isn't an inborn condition.

00:20.920 --> 00:25.300
I think you should undergo more tests
 at a specialized research lab.

00:25.820 --> 00:29.330
I can write you a recommendation
for one a ways from here.

00:45.250 --> 00:48.570
Ron    Kamonohashi's

00:45.250 --> 00:48.570
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

02:05.190 --> 02:07.650
<b>Investigation Division 1</b>

02:05.790 --> 02:07.650
You want to send <i>me</i> to Aichi?

02:07.650 --> 02:12.110
<b>#11   The Case of the Mad Chameleon Murder</b>

02:07.950 --> 02:09.330
Are you sure about that?

02:09.330 --> 02:13.320
We're slammed, so we can't spare
 any first-rate talent right now.

02:13.320 --> 02:14.860
So that's the deal...

02:18.950 --> 02:21.290
While you're there, check in on <i>him</i>.

02:21.710 --> 02:22.620
Him who?

02:22.620 --> 02:26.360
The piece of trash you ran
 that joint investigation with.

02:28.160 --> 02:30.200
You mean Eagle Eye Kawasemi-san?

02:30.200 --> 02:33.720
Ever since he lost Yamane on that case,

02:33.720 --> 02:36.980
Major Crimes' arrest rate has plummeted.

02:37.720 --> 02:42.180
<i>Oh, right. Amamiya-senpai and Kawasemi-san
were colleagues when they joined the force.</i>

02:42.800 --> 02:45.640
<i>She may be quick to call him trash,</i>

02:45.640 --> 02:46.930
<i>but deep down...</i>

02:48.360 --> 02:50.290
If this keeps up,

02:50.290 --> 02:54.760
the whispering about him becoming the perfect
 superintendent will go up in smoke!

02:54.760 --> 02:56.630
Go forth, Isshiki!

02:56.630 --> 03:00.110
Witness what the little birdies report 
of Kawasemi's swan song!

03:00.110 --> 03:01.290
<i>She's doubling down!</i>

03:04.250 --> 03:08.710
<b>...the popular black sugar dango.
They are currently being sold in the train to great...</b>

03:04.560 --> 03:08.710
So that's why I'm here.
It isn't a challenging case or anything,

03:08.710 --> 03:11.050
so why are you tagging along, Ron?

03:11.670 --> 03:14.470
Well, Kawasemi-kun's in a slump, right?

03:14.470 --> 03:17.360
Meaning a tough case might fall in our laps.

03:17.930 --> 03:21.930
So you say, but you're actually 
worried about Kawasemi-san, aren't you?

03:24.140 --> 03:26.480
I considered that line of thought, but...

03:26.480 --> 03:28.600
You're investigating your own feelings?

03:28.600 --> 03:34.290
I'm not the type of person to be invested 
in how someone else is doing.

03:34.820 --> 03:37.320
At least, I wasn't as a student.

03:39.470 --> 03:42.370
In the past, Kamonohashi Ron 
showed no weakness,

03:42.370 --> 03:44.940
and no one could get close to him.

03:44.940 --> 03:47.920
A friend who would trust him against all logic

03:47.920 --> 03:50.260
is one thing I thought he'd never have.

03:51.960 --> 03:52.960
Ron.

03:54.110 --> 03:56.750
Do you have any friends?

03:56.750 --> 03:58.430
No, not a single one.

03:58.430 --> 04:01.040
Not even one?

04:03.730 --> 04:05.100
I see.

04:06.610 --> 04:09.060
Oh. I guess you're my friend.

04:09.060 --> 04:10.890
I'm glad to hear it.

04:12.270 --> 04:17.100
<i>Just like Grizzly-san said, 
Ron is starting to change.</i>

04:22.910 --> 04:25.410
You're headed to the station, right?

04:25.410 --> 04:26.870
Let's meet up again later.

04:26.870 --> 04:29.210
Huh? Where are you going?

04:29.210 --> 04:31.180
I'm not here for fun or just because.

04:31.180 --> 04:33.590
I happen to have some business in the area.

04:39.260 --> 04:42.470
<b>Aichi Prefectural Police Headquarters</b>

04:39.260 --> 04:42.470
<b>North Wing</b>

04:42.470 --> 04:45.230
I finished my report in a jiffy,

04:45.230 --> 04:48.180
but Kawasemi-san is out on patrol right now...

04:48.180 --> 04:50.140
<b>Uramonzen Main Street</b>

04:52.100 --> 04:54.400
<i>According to the people at the station,</i>

04:52.100 --> 04:55.570
<b>Uramonzen Main Street</b>

04:54.400 --> 04:56.410
<i>Kawasemi-san should be around here.</i>

04:56.410 --> 04:58.190
You should be clean-shaven on duty!

05:02.000 --> 05:03.250
<i>Kawasemi-san!</i>

05:03.910 --> 05:05.120
Shh!

05:05.620 --> 05:08.290
Kawasemi-san, don't say that so loudly!

05:08.290 --> 05:10.120
I'm undercover right now!

05:10.120 --> 05:12.340
What? I-I'm sorry.

05:12.340 --> 05:15.840
I'm the decoy here. He's the lead.

05:17.700 --> 05:19.300
Kimyou, sir!

05:20.300 --> 05:21.800
And who are you?

05:21.800 --> 05:25.300
Before jumping in, 
you should introduce yourself!

05:25.810 --> 05:28.470
My name <i>is</i> Kimyou, sir!
But not meaning "strange"!

05:28.470 --> 05:30.430
<b>constable</b>

05:28.470 --> 05:30.430
<b>No.</b>

05:33.000 --> 05:36.150
Apologies. That's a fine last name.

05:36.150 --> 05:39.860
<i>Kawasemi-san really is making one 
uncharacteristic mistake after another.</i>

05:42.320 --> 05:43.680
You're...

05:44.300 --> 05:45.780
Hello!

05:45.780 --> 05:47.990
<b>Noodle House</b>

05:45.780 --> 05:47.990
<b>Nagomi-an</b>

05:45.780 --> 05:47.990
<b>Noodle House
Nagomi-an</b>

05:45.780 --> 05:47.990
<b>Noodle House
Nagomi-an</b>

05:47.990 --> 05:52.460
I see. So you've come to Aichi 
to report on widespread crime.

05:52.460 --> 05:54.120
That's the story,

05:54.120 --> 05:57.250
but Amamiya just wants to see
 how far I've fallen, no?

05:58.190 --> 05:59.910
H-How could you tell?

05:59.910 --> 06:02.170
Because I've known her a long time.

06:02.590 --> 06:04.540
Is that how it works?

06:04.540 --> 06:08.390
Please tell her that I'm in 
the darkest depths of a slump.

06:09.440 --> 06:12.310
The higher-ups had a lot to say 
about the incident with Yamane,

06:12.310 --> 06:15.420
which hasn't affected me 
as I don't let it bother me.

06:15.420 --> 06:19.820
And my desire to work hard enough 
to make up for this loss hasn't waned.

06:20.940 --> 06:21.830
However...

06:23.150 --> 06:26.870
I can't see everything I used to.

06:28.170 --> 06:29.830
Kawasemi-san...

06:32.060 --> 06:33.160
Oh.

06:33.160 --> 06:34.540
It's already two.

06:35.150 --> 06:36.500
You should grab souvenirs and go.

06:39.960 --> 06:42.170
<b>Osumi</b>

06:44.130 --> 06:46.650
You bought as much 
as a student on a class trip.

06:44.130 --> 06:50.100
<b>BEWARE
 the Mad
 Chameleon!</b>

06:46.650 --> 06:48.580
I know my grandma will love it, so...

06:50.100 --> 06:52.060
<b>BEWARE
 the Mad
 Chameleon!</b>

06:50.100 --> 06:52.060
<b>Merchants Association</b>

06:52.060 --> 06:54.050
The Mad Chameleon?

06:54.050 --> 06:57.020
A random attacker 
causing chaos in the area of late.

06:57.020 --> 07:00.900
In broad daylight, they hit students 
with something like a wrench,

07:00.900 --> 07:02.980
steal their smart phones, and disappear.

07:02.980 --> 07:05.430
They only take phones?

07:05.430 --> 07:07.220
Not wallets or anything?

07:07.220 --> 07:08.200
Correct.

07:08.200 --> 07:10.420
Based on trace evidence left at the scene,

07:10.420 --> 07:14.410
all of the attacks have been committed
 by the same lone perpetrator.

07:14.410 --> 07:16.180
Yet the baffling thing is that

07:16.180 --> 07:19.630
their appearance is different
 every single time.

07:20.400 --> 07:23.510
This seeming ability to change looks 
at will earned them the nickname

07:23.510 --> 07:25.090
"the Mad Chameleon."

07:27.170 --> 07:29.800
So... a master of disguise?

07:29.800 --> 07:31.760
According to the victim testimony,

07:31.760 --> 07:34.370
the culprit is a grade schooler
 with fox-like eyes,

07:34.370 --> 07:36.510
a large man close to two meters in height,

07:36.510 --> 07:38.440
a slim, elegant female office worker...

07:38.440 --> 07:40.210
It's different every time.

07:41.770 --> 07:43.250
There's no way...

07:43.250 --> 07:45.600
That's why the investigation's
 been so difficult.

08:06.920 --> 08:08.980
Isshiki, after the man in the red hoodie!

08:08.980 --> 08:11.330
I'll see to the victim 
and contact the station!

08:11.330 --> 08:12.140
Yes, sir!

08:23.690 --> 08:25.480
<b>No Right Turns Ahead</b>

08:23.690 --> 08:25.480
<b>No pedestrian passage due to construction</b>

08:26.200 --> 08:27.270
Are you all right?

08:27.950 --> 08:29.910
How savage!

08:33.160 --> 08:36.330
<b>CLOTHIER</b>

08:39.640 --> 08:42.640
I've detained everyone who was in the shop,

08:43.230 --> 08:45.900
but none of them are wearing a red hoodie.

08:46.600 --> 08:49.240
I think he took it off and hid it, but...

08:49.880 --> 08:52.670
If you want to hide a tree, 
hide it in a forest.

08:53.100 --> 08:55.770
The victim was a local university student.

08:55.770 --> 08:57.990
He was just confirmed dead.

08:59.320 --> 09:00.560
That's awful...

09:00.560 --> 09:03.640
And it means this is now
 a murder investigation.

09:03.640 --> 09:04.770
Sir!

09:04.770 --> 09:09.340
Isshiki, can you definitively prove
that the culprit hasn't left this shop?

09:09.340 --> 09:10.490
Yes, sir.

09:10.800 --> 09:14.020
The emergency exit is 
completely blocked by boxes,

09:14.470 --> 09:18.320
and we've confirmed there's no other
 way out apart from the front entrance.

09:18.890 --> 09:20.120
I see.

09:21.810 --> 09:22.720
That means...

09:23.080 --> 09:25.430
the Mad Chameleon is here among us.

09:26.500 --> 09:27.350
What?

09:27.920 --> 09:30.170
<b>Osumi</b>

09:28.540 --> 09:30.170
Striking in broad daylight...

09:30.640 --> 09:32.130
Wielding a wrench...

09:32.130 --> 09:34.330
Targeting university students...

09:34.850 --> 09:39.360
And stealing the victim's phone...

09:40.610 --> 09:43.300
This matches the previous attacks to a tee.

09:44.020 --> 09:46.060
And now the culprit's crossed the line.

09:48.400 --> 09:50.240
I'll have a look at these men.

09:50.590 --> 09:51.700
Sir.

09:51.700 --> 09:54.410
<i>Here it comes! Kawasemi-san's...</i>

09:54.410 --> 09:55.810
<i>eagle eyes in action!</i>

09:58.260 --> 10:00.280
<i>An elementary student with fox-like eyes?</i>

10:00.900 --> 10:01.790
<i>No.</i>

10:04.400 --> 10:06.420
<i>An elegant office worker?</i>

10:09.280 --> 10:11.380
<i>A man close to two meters in height?</i>

10:22.450 --> 10:23.580
I can't see anything.

10:28.020 --> 10:29.360
Ron

10:29.360 --> 10:33.570
<b>National Neurological Research Center</b>

10:30.320 --> 10:33.570
Hey, Toto. Did you see Kawasemi-kun?

10:33.570 --> 10:37.280
About that... There was a murder
right in front of us. It's awful!

10:38.990 --> 10:40.680
A murder?

10:42.660 --> 10:44.160
I see.

10:44.160 --> 10:46.310
It's not a matter of disguise.

10:46.310 --> 10:48.550
They couldn't change their physique like that.

10:48.550 --> 10:50.630
<i>What? Then...</i>

10:51.680 --> 10:53.380
If it isn't disguises,

10:53.380 --> 10:58.810
then why does the Mad Chameleon look 
completely different to everyone who sees them?

10:59.590 --> 11:02.690
"Why"? Are you asking me?

11:02.690 --> 11:03.520
<i>No.</i>

11:04.020 --> 11:06.230
I'll head there now. Just wait.

11:11.480 --> 11:13.940
<b>CLOTHIER</b>

11:13.940 --> 11:17.190
We've checked the security cameras 
in the shopping arcade,

11:17.190 --> 11:19.100
but between the crowd and his hat and mask,

11:19.100 --> 11:22.300
there's no clear picture
 of the culprit's face.

11:22.300 --> 11:25.330
If only there were cameras in this shop...

11:25.330 --> 11:27.530
Regardless, according to forensics,

11:27.530 --> 11:30.560
from the angle of the laceration 
to the back of the victim's head,

11:30.560 --> 11:34.030
the culprit is at least one hundred 
and seventy centimeters tall.

11:34.030 --> 11:35.300
I only saw him from afar,

11:35.300 --> 11:38.690
but the man in the red hoodie 
was around that height.

11:40.310 --> 11:41.440
In other words...

11:41.920 --> 11:45.510
We can narrow the suspects down to three men.

11:46.310 --> 11:49.130
Even as I am now, 
I may be able to see something.

12:11.560 --> 12:13.670
It's no use. I see nothing.

12:14.500 --> 12:16.130
Kawasemi-san...

12:16.130 --> 12:19.570
We've finished taking their statements. 
There's nothing unusual in them.

12:19.570 --> 12:22.850
We've taken down their names 
and contact information.

12:22.850 --> 12:23.940
What should we do?

12:24.630 --> 12:26.810
For now, you can let them go.

12:29.520 --> 12:31.530
Man, what a pain.

12:31.530 --> 12:33.980
What's with that quack of a detective?

12:34.480 --> 12:36.440
This is the state I'm in, Isshiki.

12:37.010 --> 12:39.060
You must think my
"Eagle Eye" moniker ludicrous.

12:39.060 --> 12:40.500
Don't say that...

12:41.410 --> 12:43.160
Sounds like you're in a real bind,

12:43.160 --> 12:44.620
Kawasemi-kun.

12:44.990 --> 12:46.380
Ron!

12:47.290 --> 12:49.160
We've caught a suspicious man!

12:49.160 --> 12:51.300
<i>You're</i> the one in a bind!

12:53.210 --> 12:55.030
So you came, too?

12:55.420 --> 12:58.330
I believe you said your name 
was Tekemono Kamomi.

12:58.650 --> 13:01.380
No. I'm sorry, but today I am...

13:05.060 --> 13:06.700
Nearsighted Kamosemi.

13:06.700 --> 13:08.520
Are you <i>trying</i> to make him angry?!

13:08.520 --> 13:10.200
No need for theatrics.

13:10.200 --> 13:12.210
Lend me your skills, Kamosemi.

13:12.210 --> 13:13.230
What?

13:13.230 --> 13:17.190
I believe I've already told you
that I understand you two.

13:17.970 --> 13:20.400
<i>The Hand Collector murder case...</i>

13:20.400 --> 13:23.390
<i>He knows it was Ron 
who solved that and not me.</i>

13:23.390 --> 13:26.030
<i>Impressive as ever, Kawasemi-san!</i>

13:26.030 --> 13:30.190
You've already heard the details 
from Isshiki, haven't you?

13:30.190 --> 13:33.500
Well, since you insist, 
I have a few questions first.

13:33.900 --> 13:36.690
I heard the victim was a university student,

13:36.690 --> 13:38.590
so what was he doing in a suit?

13:38.590 --> 13:42.260
I don't know. It may be another case 
of returning home after job hunting.

13:42.260 --> 13:43.050
Another?

13:43.050 --> 13:43.820
Yes.

13:44.240 --> 13:48.530
Of the previous victims, two were 
on their way back from job hunting.

13:49.560 --> 13:51.650
The others were a mock exam supervisor

13:51.650 --> 13:53.660
and a part-time office worker.

13:55.520 --> 13:57.020
So you're saying...

13:57.020 --> 13:59.990
They were all wearing suits, weren't they?

14:01.120 --> 14:02.290
Now that you mention it...

14:02.290 --> 14:03.700
What's the deal?

14:05.160 --> 14:09.620
That is the great mystery which will lead 
to the true identity of the Mad Chameleon!

14:10.580 --> 14:13.060
The culprit's appearance changes every time.

14:13.060 --> 14:16.590
If it's not disguises,
 there's only one explanation.

14:17.120 --> 14:20.800
All of the victims are lying.

14:20.800 --> 14:21.760
What?!

14:21.760 --> 14:23.450
Th-They're lying?

14:23.450 --> 14:26.400
But they were the ones who were attacked!

14:26.400 --> 14:28.160
Why would they lie?

14:28.160 --> 14:30.430
A guilty conscience, perhaps.

14:32.840 --> 14:37.030
There was a reason those university 
student victims were wearing suits.

14:37.030 --> 14:39.360
And from that we can deduce...

14:39.710 --> 14:40.880
Don't tell me...

14:40.880 --> 14:41.820
Huh?

14:41.820 --> 14:43.530
An "it's me" scam?!

14:44.990 --> 14:47.200
Huh? What do you mean?

14:47.200 --> 14:50.450
All of the victims were money
 collectors in a type of scam.

14:51.200 --> 14:53.520
In order to pose as bank 
employees or the like,

14:53.520 --> 14:56.000
they went around during the day in suits.

14:56.000 --> 15:00.550
That would explain this seemingly 
random series of attacks.

15:00.550 --> 15:01.960
I get it!

15:02.260 --> 15:04.370
If the culprit is caught,

15:04.370 --> 15:07.440
it'd expose that they're all 
connected to this scam!

15:07.440 --> 15:10.120
That's why the victims lied!

15:10.120 --> 15:14.680
The culprit has to be someone 
connecting the money collectors.

15:14.680 --> 15:17.270
In other words, a member of the con.

15:18.050 --> 15:22.370
There was likely trouble over money
 or something within the group.

15:23.250 --> 15:25.810
The reason the culprit took their phones

15:25.810 --> 15:27.840
was to eliminate all trace of contact

15:27.840 --> 15:29.440
with the group perpetrating the con.

15:32.100 --> 15:34.750
Very impressive, Kamosemi.

15:35.380 --> 15:37.460
As I suspected, you're no ordinary man.

15:37.460 --> 15:38.780
You think so?

15:38.780 --> 15:43.680
The real you would've picked up on something 
like this long before now, you know?

15:46.000 --> 15:49.600
It's your turn, Eagle Eye Kawasemi.

15:53.480 --> 15:56.890
I would very much like to, 
but right now, I can't...

15:56.890 --> 16:00.530
But you're the only one
 who can arrest the culprit.

16:00.530 --> 16:04.700
If you insist it's impossible, 
then I, Nearsighted Kamosemi...

16:05.320 --> 16:07.280
will scold you with my tongs!

16:07.280 --> 16:09.610
You're stealing his tweezer thing?!

16:11.510 --> 16:13.120
You haven't been sleeping!

16:15.080 --> 16:16.980
And you haven't been eating properly!

16:17.540 --> 16:22.750
Your tanking performance continues 
to betray Yamane, who idolized you.

16:27.450 --> 16:29.960
I-I've been trying my hardest.

16:30.850 --> 16:34.320
So no one caves under the pressure 
like Yamane did,

16:34.320 --> 16:36.890
I've been careful 
with every correction I give!

16:36.890 --> 16:39.350
See? That's your mistake.

16:40.260 --> 16:43.980
One could say you've become 
a mistake-filled Demon Lord of mistakes.

16:47.350 --> 16:48.490
Wait.

16:49.920 --> 16:52.950
"Mistake-filled"? You are the one person...

16:53.400 --> 16:55.290
I don't want to hear that from!

16:55.290 --> 16:56.890
I can't hold back anymore!

16:57.300 --> 16:58.460
Your necktie is too long!

16:59.410 --> 17:01.370
These price tags are still attached!

17:02.200 --> 17:03.920
Your socks don't match!

17:03.920 --> 17:05.590
And your shoes are even worse!

17:05.590 --> 17:07.300
He's returning the scolding?

17:07.300 --> 17:09.840
<i>But Ron </i>is<i> dressed unbelievably badly!</i>

17:11.020 --> 17:12.520
And that's not all!

17:13.580 --> 17:14.430
<i>Wait...</i>

17:14.430 --> 17:17.140
Don't put an unwrapped 
tempura onigiri in your pocket!

17:18.610 --> 17:20.850
<i>Somehow, Kawasemi-san...</i>

17:21.940 --> 17:23.510
<i>looks like he's come alive!</i>

17:24.310 --> 17:27.650
You said you're nearsighted, 
but those glasses are for farsightedness!

17:30.610 --> 17:32.830
See? You can do it when you try.

17:33.570 --> 17:38.090
Now, just turn those eagle eyes 
on the three men from earlier.

17:52.150 --> 17:53.730
Kawasemi-san?

17:58.640 --> 18:00.050
Isshiki.

18:00.050 --> 18:01.620
As the man in the red hoodie fled,

18:01.620 --> 18:04.210
you said he rammed a pedestrian 
with his elbow, yes?

18:04.210 --> 18:05.660
Y-Yes.

18:05.660 --> 18:07.570
Was it his left arm?

18:07.570 --> 18:10.040
Um... Yes, it was.

18:10.040 --> 18:11.030
Where did it happen?

18:11.030 --> 18:13.150
At the entrance to the crossroads.

18:13.150 --> 18:14.290
As I thought.

18:14.990 --> 18:17.200
The culprit didn't ram anyone.

18:17.370 --> 18:25.220
<b>No Right Turns Ahead</b>

18:18.160 --> 18:20.900
He saw the sign about restricted
access at certain times.

18:20.900 --> 18:23.330
He was just checking his watch!

18:23.330 --> 18:24.280
What?

18:24.290 --> 18:35.780
<b>No Entry
Due to Construction
Thank you</b>

18:24.720 --> 18:28.110
He thought he'd be able to get through,

18:28.110 --> 18:30.270
but the path was already closed,

18:30.270 --> 18:32.450
leaving him no choice but to hide here!

18:32.880 --> 18:35.590
What? How could he screw up like that?

18:37.680 --> 18:39.180
Because his watch...

18:40.140 --> 18:41.850
was malfunctioning!

18:44.080 --> 18:48.510
Of the three men, only one 
was wearing a malfunctioning watch.

18:49.320 --> 18:50.890
He's the culprit!

18:51.280 --> 18:53.490
<b>No Right Turns Ahead</b>

18:51.280 --> 18:53.490
<b>No pedestrian passage due to construction</b>

18:53.490 --> 18:55.950
<b>No Entry
Due to Construction
Thank you</b>

18:55.570 --> 18:58.710
No luck. The culprit's license
 was counterfeit.

18:58.710 --> 19:00.530
His number and address are fake, too.

19:00.530 --> 19:01.790
That can't be!

19:01.790 --> 19:02.910
It's all right.

19:03.330 --> 19:06.940
We did not find 
the victim's smart phone on him.

19:06.940 --> 19:08.380
Which means...

19:09.550 --> 19:12.030
he must have hidden it 
somewhere in this store.

19:12.030 --> 19:14.090
He will not fail to return to retrieve it.

19:14.090 --> 19:17.690
We found the red hoodie 
in a clothes bag on a shelf.

19:17.690 --> 19:20.750
But we can't find the smart phone anywhere.

19:20.750 --> 19:22.510
Where could it be?

19:23.960 --> 19:25.100
It's simple.

19:26.310 --> 19:28.880
We've already seen it.

19:29.860 --> 19:32.160
The smart phone you're looking for...

19:33.490 --> 19:35.320
is in the middle of a call.

19:38.170 --> 19:40.460
Huh? What's that supposed to mean?

19:45.790 --> 19:47.420
I see.

19:47.420 --> 19:50.380
<b>Osumi</b>

20:16.950 --> 20:18.840
Don't move! Police!

20:24.760 --> 20:26.920
Giving it to a mannequin to hold...

20:26.920 --> 20:29.290
What a clever hiding place.

20:36.920 --> 20:39.880
You are under arrest on suspicion of murder,

20:39.880 --> 20:41.380
Mad Chameleon!

20:48.020 --> 20:50.400
Wait, that's strange.

20:50.400 --> 20:52.140
Sir! I said that's not my name!

20:52.140 --> 20:53.100
I didn't mean you!

20:55.980 --> 20:58.540
You can't fool my eagle eyes.

20:59.700 --> 21:00.920
Constable Kimyou!

21:03.630 --> 21:05.580
Your necktie...

21:06.230 --> 21:07.540
is five millimeters askew.

22:47.050 --> 22:49.760
<b>...inside the train cars.
This train is bound for Tokyo...</b>

22:52.730 --> 22:56.180
Kawasemi-san said they have the Mad 
Chameleon secured and under arrest.

22:56.180 --> 22:57.440
Isn't that great, Ron?

22:57.440 --> 23:00.230
Huh? I had nothing to do with it.

23:01.680 --> 23:03.730
<i>He just can't be honest with his feelings.</i>

23:03.730 --> 23:06.740
Oh, right. What was that business 
you had to take care of?

23:06.740 --> 23:11.150
Oh, I went to a neurological 
research center that's in Aichi.

23:11.150 --> 23:12.160
What?

23:12.160 --> 23:16.420
The other day, I had Mofu-sensei take a 
look at me and my "killing culprits disease,"

23:16.420 --> 23:19.350
and it turns out
 more detailed tests are in order.

23:19.350 --> 23:21.130
She gave me a recommendation.

23:21.130 --> 23:23.440
Huh? You mean <i>the</i> Mofu-sensei?

23:23.440 --> 23:25.340
That's what you were doing?

23:28.090 --> 23:33.370
Apparently, depending on the diagnosis, 
there may be a way to alleviate my symptoms.

23:33.370 --> 23:34.560
Really?!

23:34.560 --> 23:37.020
Wow! That's great news, Ron!

23:37.020 --> 23:39.980
Oh, come on! You should be celebrating!
